PLC-573P-01 → (Programmable Logic Controller — not ISA instrument)        confidence: 0.0

CRITICAL RULE — Equipment tag vs Instrument tag:
  Equipment tags: SINGLE uppercase letter + hyphen + number  →  P-101, V-201, D-101, E-301
  These are NEVER instruments. Do NOT interpret P as Pressure, V as Vibration, D as Density.
  The single letter before the hyphen is a VESSEL/EQUIPMENT CLASS CODE, NOT an ISA variable letter.
  V-201 is a VESSEL (equipment) — it is NOT a "Vibration Indicator".
  D-101 is a DRUM (equipment)  — it is NOT a "Density" anything.
  P-101 is a PUMP (equipment)  — it is NOT a "Pressure" anything.

CRITICAL RULE — Bare single/double letters are ALWAYS noise (conf 0.0):
  If the ENTIRE tag is just one or two characters with no number → it is OCR noise.
  A  alone  → NOT "Analysis" — it is a fragment, confidence: 0.0
  I  alone  → NOT "Indicator" — it is a fragment, confidence: 0.0
  M  alone  → NOT "Motor" — it is a fragment, confidence: 0.0
  CC alone  → NOT "Conductivity Controller" — it is a fragment, confidence: 0.0
  The ISA first-letter decode ONLY applies when the tag has a number suffix (e.g., AT-101, FIC-202).
  A bare letter without a loop number is ALWAYS noise.

CRITICAL RULE — Electrical equipment (not ISA-5.1 instruments):
  VFD (Variable Frequency Drive), PLC (Programmable Logic Controller),
  MCC (Motor Control Centre), UPS, DCS (when used as a tag, not a system label)
  → These are electrical/automation equipment. confidence: 0.0

══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
SECTION 12 — RESPONSE FORMAT
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ALWAYS return exactly this JSON — no extra text, no explanation:

{
  "description": "<concise instrument name>",
  "io_type": "<one of: AI, AO, DI, DO, Soft Link, ''>",
  "system": "<one of: DCS, SIS/ESD, F&GS, ''>",
  "confidence": <0.0 to 1.0>
}

Confidence scale:
  1.0 = exact match to examples table or a standard ISA code
  0.8 = derived from ISA-5.1 letter rules with high certainty
  0.6 = reasonable inference from partial pattern or loop context
  0.4 = best guess, ambiguous code
  0.0 = NOT an instrument (annotation, noise, equipment tag, symbol)

For non-instruments:
  {"description": "", "io_type": "", "system": "", "confidence": 0.0}
"""

